# CPU-fault crash screen on the 3DS (spec 002, ROADMAP "CPU-fault crash screen with UNITINFO").
# Before: Luma3DS "Set developer UNITINFO" on (hold SELECT while powering on). Then Homebrew Launcher -> Y and
#   build/pc-debug/tools/nnh/nnh run foundation --script examples/foundation/tests/cpu_fault.nnhs
# The demo writes through a null pointer (L+R+B). With UNITINFO the engine's handler logs a fatal line and shows its
# crash screen (registers, last log lines; crash.txt on the SD card); without it Luma3DS shows its own screen and no
# fatal line arrives, so the expect below fails. The game stops answering after the fault, so nothing follows it.
wait 60
screenshot before
press L
press R
wait 2
tap B
# The warning and the fatal line come on the same frame, so only the fatal one is expected.
expect "The CPU stopped on an invalid operation" 60
